Lobium — exact-build native fingerprint capability contract.

Adds --lobium-fingerprint-capabilities. The executable itself prints the versioned JSON contract before
browser startup, so the sidecar probes the exact binary it will spawn instead of trusting a filename,
package label, or stale sidecar manifest. Any older/unpatched Chromium build has no contract and profile
launch fails closed.

The capability LIST is not written here. It lives in components/lobium_fp/lobium_capabilities.cc, next
to the hooks it describes, because a list duplicated into a patch literal drifts: adding a hook and
forgetting the literal under-reports, while editing the literal without adding the hook makes the binary
claim spoofing it does not have — and the sidecar trusts that claim. Keeping this patch to a single call
means the hook inventory changes in one place, and ci/validation/patch-series.test.mjs cross-checks that
place against both patches/series and packages/engine-runner/src/lobium-capabilities.ts.

diff --git a/chrome/app/chrome_main.cc b/chrome/app/chrome_main.cc
index f3c06b9e10d09..7f1770b1b0886 100644
--- a/chrome/app/chrome_main.cc
+++ b/chrome/app/chrome_main.cc
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include "build/build_config.h"
 #if !defined(BUILDING_CHROME_RENDERER)
 #include "chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.h"
+#include "components/lobium_fp/lobium_capabilities.h"
 #endif
 #include "chrome/app/startup_timestamps.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/headless/headless_mode_init.h"
@@ -196,6 +197,19 @@ int ChromeMain(int argc, const char** argv) {
 
   base::CommandLine* command_line(base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess());
 
+  // Lobium: machine-readable proof of the native fingerprint hooks in THIS executable. The sidecar
+  // runs this before every first launch of a binary (then caches by path/size/mtime) and rejects a
+  // missing/incompatible capability. Emitted before any browser startup work so the probe stays
+  // cheap, and on stdout alone so the sidecar can parse it as exact JSON.
+  //
+  // The list itself lives in components/lobium_fp/lobium_capabilities.cc, beside the hooks it
+  // describes - a copy here would drift, and a manifest that over-reports is worse than none,
+  // because the sidecar launches on the strength of it.
+  if (command_line->HasSwitch("lobium-fingerprint-capabilities")) {
+    std::cout << lobium::CapabilityManifestJson() << std::endl;
+    return 0;
+  }
+
   // Capture the unpolluted command line snapshot in the browser process.
   // This must happen immediately after CommandLine::Init to ensure we capture
   // the state before any internal programmatic mutations.
